  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The All Progressives Congress (APC) in Zamfara State has resumed its campaign activities following a period of mourning for 15 supporters who died in a road accident. The tragedy previously forced the party to postpone its rally in Maru. During the recent campaign event in Shinkafi, notable party figures such as the Director General of the Tinubu/Shettima Presidential Campaign Council and former Governor Abdul'aziz Yari were in attendance. The gathered leadership focused on pledging new infrastructure, health, and education projects for the region. These developments occur amid broader national campaign efforts, which have seen various party representatives and government officials navigating logistical and political challenges, including incidents involving transport safety and requests for community support across various Nigerian states as the 2027 election cycle progresses.",
